---
// The docs front page: a short overview that says what each page covers and
// where to start. The sidebar already lists every page, so this doesn't.
import { getCollection } from 'astro:content';
import Docs from '../../layouts/Docs.astro';
// releases.md arrives with the release it describes, so it is linked only
// once a published nightly has shipped it (as the sidebar does).
const hasReleases = (await getCollection('docs')).some((d) => d.id === 'releases');
---

<Docs
  title="Docs"
  fullTitle="Pulsar docs: install, updates, gaming and agents"
  description="How to install and use Pulsar, with pages on themes, games, coding agents, updates and rollback, troubleshooting, and how each image is built and signed."
  path="/docs"
>
  <h1>Pulsar docs</h1>
  <p class="intro">
    If you’re new to Pulsar, start with <a href="/docs/install">Install</a>. If you’re moving from
    Windows or a Mac, <a href="/docs/coming-from">From Windows or macOS</a> covers making the USB stick
    on the system you have now, keeping Windows alongside, and where your apps and shortcuts went.
  </p>
  <p>
    The system is one read-only image, so software goes in different places than on most Linux
    systems. <a href="/docs/where-things-go">Where things go</a> says where apps, dev tools and
    services belong. <a href="/docs/themes">Themes</a> and <a href="/docs/theming">How theming works</a>{' '}
    cover the look. <a href="/docs/gaming">Gaming</a> covers Steam and the other launchers, and{' '}
    <a href="/docs/gamescale">gamescale</a> runs games at your screen’s real resolution while
    fractional scaling is on. On the NVIDIA image, <a href="/docs/gpu-containers">GPU containers</a>{' '}
    shows how to run CUDA and local models in podman.
  </p>
  <p>
    <a href="/docs/agents">Coding agents</a> shows how to install Claude Code, Codex and the others,
    and <a href="/docs/agents-safety">Agents and safety</a> says what an agent can change without
    asking.
  </p>
  <p>
    Updates download in the background and apply when you restart.{' '}
    <a href="/docs/updates">Updates and rollback</a> covers how that works and how to go back. When
    something breaks, run <code>pulsar doctor</code> first, then read{' '}
    <a href="/docs/troubleshooting">Troubleshooting</a>. <a href="/docs/cli">The pulsar command</a>{' '}
    lists every subcommand.
  </p>
  <p>
    <a href="/docs/signing">Signing</a> and <a href="/docs/provenance">Provenance</a> explain how each
    image is built and signed, and how to check it yourself.
    {hasReleases && (
      <>
        {' '}The <a href="/docs/releases">release notes</a> list what’s new in each Pulsar release.
      </>
    )}{' '}
    <a href="/docs/changelog">Nightly builds</a> lists every package that changed in the latest build.
  </p>
</Docs>

<style>
  .intro {
    font-size: var(--text-lg);
    max-width: 56ch;
  }
</style>
